commit/3b9ab909a13b7081b60bd524a6283638482212cd","commit_subject":"karate-core: configure maxResponseSize and maxHeaderSize. A response body over maxResponseSize bytes fails the request with \"Maximum response size reached\" (postman-request's text), read through a bounded stream, a compressed body counted as decoded; the status line and headers over maxHeaderSize bytes fail it with \"Header overflow: the response headers are over N bytes\", and the limit is also each header line's (httpclient5's own line limit, 8 KB by default, otherwise refuses a longer header line with MessageConstraintException, which now reads as the same overflow). Unset (null) is no limit; a negative value is refused. maxHeaderSize is part of the client's key, since it shapes the connection factory; maxResponseSize is read per response, as strictResponseParsing is. Karate's Postman runner maps postman-runtime's maxResponseSize and maxHeaderSize onto them. DESIGN.md lists both keys. Gate: karate-core 3090 tests, 0 failures after KarateConfigCopyTest learned long fields (ApacheHttpClientResponseLimitsTest new).","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"openfootmanager/openfootmanager","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:52:15Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"568914c0db36309157278fbe2fe4f19b97ce93e3","github_link":"https://github.com/openfootmanager/openfootmanager/commit/568914c0db36309157278fbe2fe4f19b97ce93e3","commit_subject":"feat(lib): one client-side row sorter for the lists the backend sends whole","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"cypress-io/cypress-design","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:52:04Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"bcca539126b0496c9cca080b6e812f415dbf6270","github_link":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress-design/commit/bcca539126b0496c9cca080b6e812f415dbf6270","commit_subject":"docs(icon): correct instructions against the code (#798)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"karakeep-app/karakeep","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:51:47Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"6c95c14ab7d9de8a